        "node_id": "n_3_48d542",
        "thought_text": "Mathematical optimization: Instead of checking all possible rectangles, we can use the properties of the product matrix to reduce the search space. For example, if a rectangle sum is equal to a, then the sum of its corners must be divisible by a. This allows us to precompute valid corner combinations and use them to count rectangles more efficiently.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
